WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back
to "the tonight show."

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.436
We're about to play
a brand-new game.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.704
This is "Fake Off."

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:09.509
-♪ Aah, fake off ♪

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.910
♪ Fake off ♪

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.845
-I'm going to need some help
on this one,

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:17.684
so joining me now is the one
and only Kevin James!

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.119 line:0%
Kevin, it is great to see you.
-Thank you.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.054 line:0%
-Thank you for playing this game
with me.

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.891 line:0%
Here's how this works --
Kevin and I are each

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.225 line:0%
going to take turns presenting

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.361 line:0%
three projects
that we worked on.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.463 line:0%
The catch is that one of them
is completely fake.

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.565 line:0%
We'll ask each other questions
and try to figure out

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:34.834 line:0%
which one is made up.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.702 line:0%
And if we get it right,
we win that round.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:38.137 line:0%
Sound good?
-Okay.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:41.340 line:0%
All right. You ready?
-Yep.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.343
-Which of these is not a real
movie I starred in, okay?

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.613
"A," "Grilled."

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.950
-Uh-huh.
"B," "The Dog House."

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.455
Or "C," "True Memoirs of
an International Assassin."

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:59.692
-I saw "True Memoirs,"
so that's real.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:03.295
"The Dog House" feels like

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.064
that's not something you would
have done.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.232
"Grilled," who is that in there
with you in "Grilled?"

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:10.470
I can't --
-It was Ray Romano.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.374
-Oh, well I think you and Ray
know each other from standup.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.309
And I should see "Grilled"
by the way if that --

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:20.580
I would say I don't believe that
you were in "The Dog House."

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.915
I think that is not a --
I believe you have been

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.717
in the dog house
in your real life.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.720
-Right.
-But I say that is a fake movie.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.557
-"The Dog House" is fake.
All right, you're correct.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.223
[ Ding! ]
You're right.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.692
It is the fake one.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.661
I'm kind of mad. I wanted you
to jump on -- "The Dog House."

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.697
It's sad that "The Dog House"
is something that could be

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:41.200
considered something I did,
right?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.869
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.305
-No. Wait,
what would be the concept?

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.141
Do you somehow --
like your wife put --

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.742
You're in the dog house,
and so you actually start

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.311
living in the dog house?"
-Yes. With the dog.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:55.982
And it becomes a buddy movie
between me and a dog.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.416
It's got to be a buddy movie.
Right?

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:59.685
I do something,
the wife gets upset with me,

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.754
I'm out in the dog house,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.357
and then we form a relationship,
and we go on the road somehow.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:08.861
And he fixes me, and
I come back, and all is well.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.130
-Okay, here we go.
Back to me now.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.598
These questions.
-Okay.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.267
-Which of these is not
a real album of mine?

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.303
I don't know if you knew
I had albums.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.239
Is it "A,"
"Blow Your Pants Off."

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.643
"B," "The Bathroom Wall."

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.512
Or "C," "Greatest Hit."

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.015
-Okay.
I know "The Bathroom Wall."

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:32.685
So I know that one's good.
It's between "A" and "C."

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.688
I'm going to go with
"Blow Your Pants Off."

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.056
I don't think you did that.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.359
I don't think you did
"Blow Your Pants Off."

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.826
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.395
-You're wrong. I did do that!

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.164
-Get out of here!
When did you do --

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:49.135
-I won a Grammy.
-For "Blow Your Pants Off?"

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.704
-Yeah.
-And "Bathroom Wall" nothing?

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:56.142
-[ Laughs ]
"Bathroom wall" nothing.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.777
"Blow Your Pants Off."
-That's -- Wait a second.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.778
There's a bigger story here.

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:02.815
And it's about "Bathroom Wall"
nothing.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.751
I'm happy for you
for "Blowing Your Pants Off,"

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:08.454
and good job.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.823
This is --
It's just not fair, man.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.393
-Thank you, finally.
We can call the Academy

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:17.363
and talk to somebody.
-Oh, man!

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.597
-All right, Kevin, time for the
final round.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:21.534
This is for you. You ask
a question about yourself.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.836
And if I get this right,
I'm the winner.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.738
-All right, here we go.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.374
Which of these is not
a real animated character

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:30.976
I voiced in a movie?"

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:34.947
"A," Old Man Meehan.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:38.384
"B," Otis the Cow.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.720
Or "C," Officer Landers.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.457
-[ Sighs ] This is insane.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:50.129
Is not a real animated character
you voice in a movie.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.498
Old man Meehan?

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.668
Hm. Otto the Cow.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.336
That's pretty cute.
-Otis the Cow.

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:58.771
-Sorry. Otis the Cow.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.272
-That was a trick question.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.542
I just wanted to see
if you reacted. You did.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.543
You took the bait on that one.
-Nice setup.

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:06.145
Nice setup.
-No problem.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:09.315
So that one's real.
Officer Landers.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:12.784
That seems a little fakey name,
Officer Landers.

00:04:12.784 --> 00:04:16.455
And you just played an officer
in "Hubie Halloween."

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:19.458
You're not one to repeat roles.
-Right.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.194
-I'm going to say the answer
is...

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:23.629
But yet, you're not old.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.498
Why would you play
Old Man Meehan?

00:04:26.498 --> 00:04:28.534
-Well...
-You're young.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.437
I'm going to switch
and go flip mode.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.539
I'm going to say
Old Man Meehan, fake.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.242
You never did it.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.144
-You're a son of --
You're right.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.878
You're right, man.
[ Ding ]

00:04:39.878 --> 00:04:42.648
I thought I had you on Landers.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.783
-I almost got on Landers.

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.419
What was officer Landers?
-You got me -- almost got me

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.988
on Landers,
and now I want to play Meehan.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.256
I want to play him.
-You're not old enough.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:52.925
You shouldn't play
Old Man anybody.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.727
-But you can do the
[ Old man voice ] old man voice

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.162
[ Normal voice ]
or, you know, whatever it is.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.464
I don't know what he sounds
like, but I'd like to dig in.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.066
-Well, apparently he sounds
like -- [ Grumbling ]

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.069
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.436
That gravelly...

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:05.938
-[ Gravelly voice ]
It's a gravelly old guy.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:09.542
-[ Gravelly, old man voice ] My
old man is that type of voice.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.644
-[ Old man voice ] Oh, yeah,
you can go that way, as well.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.980
-Yes. Oh, yours is British.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.616
-It -- did he -- Was he British?

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:19.051
-What do you mean?
Of course he was.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.953
-Righto.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.856
That was -- thank you
for playing our game.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.691
I got to know you
a little better.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.426
-Yeah, you did. And I know you,

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.328
and I'm still pissed off
at "Bathroom Wall."

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:32.231
Okay, buddy? I'm just --
This is just unacceptable.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.900
I'm making some phone calls.

